---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { brand } from '../config/brand';

/**
 * Written from what this site actually does, not from a template. If the site
 * gains analytics, a CRM, embedded video or any third-party script, this page
 * has to change in the same commit.
 */
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy"
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  updated="21 September 2026"
  description="What MISE OPS does with the information you send through this site. No cookies, no advertising trackers, no mailing list."
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This site sets <strong>no cookies</strong>, loads <strong>no advertising or social
    trackers</strong>, and has <strong>no mailing list</strong> to add you to. The only
    personal information we hold is what you type into the walkthrough form and send us
    deliberately.
  </p>

  <h2>What you send us</h2>
  <p>
    The Operations Walkthrough form asks for your name, restaurant name, email, phone,
    city, rough size of your operation, how you would like to be contacted, and a
    description of what is frustrating you operationally. You choose what to put in it.
  </p>
  <p>
    We use it for one thing: to reply to you and to prepare for a walkthrough. We do not
    sell it, rent it, share it with advertisers, or use it to market anything other than
    the conversation you asked for.
  </p>

  <h3>Where it goes</h3>
  <p>
    Form submissions are handled by <strong>Netlify Forms</strong>, the service that also
    hosts this site. Your submission is stored in our Netlify account and emailed to us.
    Netlify processes it on our behalf under their own privacy terms.
  </p>

  <h3>How long we keep it</h3>
  <p>
    As long as the conversation is live, and for a reasonable period afterwards in case
    you come back. Ask us to delete it and we will, and we will confirm when it is done.
  </p>

  <h2>What the site collects automatically</h2>
  <p>
    Netlify keeps standard server logs for every site it hosts — IP address, the page
    requested, timestamp, browser user-agent. That is infrastructure logging, not
    something we analyse, and we do not build profiles from it.
  </p>

  <h3>Cookies and browser storage</h3>
  <p>
    None. This site does not set cookies, does not use local storage or session storage,
    and does not fingerprint your browser. There is no cookie banner because there is
    nothing to consent to.
  </p>

  <h3>Fonts and third-party requests</h3>
  <p>
    The typefaces are served from this site’s own domain rather than from Google Fonts or
    any other CDN, so loading a page does not tell a third party that you visited.
  </p>

  <h3>Analytics</h3>
  <p>
    The site is built so that a privacy-preserving, cookie-free analytics tool could be
    switched on later — the kind that counts page views without identifying anyone.
    <strong>Nothing is currently loaded.</strong> If that changes, this page changes with
    it, and it will never be a tool that tracks you across other websites.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Ask what we hold about you, and we will tell you.</li>
    <li>Ask us to correct it or delete it, and we will.</li>
    <li>Ask us to stop contacting you, and we will stop.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    One email is enough for any of these:
    <a class="link" href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>. No form to fill in.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is for restaurant owners and operators. It is not directed at children, and
    we do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 16.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this page changes, the date at the top changes. We will not quietly broaden what we
    do with your information and leave the date alone.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about any of this go to
    <a class="link" href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
